There seems to be a bug in the Atari ST port, don't know whether it's
universal or not.  (Or even, known but now fixed, since I think the ST
version is a subrelease behind.)

Twice now, I've had really (no, **REALLY**) promising looking games
pulled out from under my feet.  In both cases, the circumstances
involved my pet attacking a 'swallowing' monster (vortex, or some
such).

The first was a week or so ago, when my current pet was (apparently) a
chameleon or some other shape-changer.  When it first came at me from a
corridor, it was a jackal.  I was a bit low on hit points and was in a
doorway defending myself from attack from the room, so I tamed it.
After a couple of moves, it turned into something else.  Ah, I said,
probably a polymorph trap, better watch out.  However, it kept
changing.  We got to a room containing a vortex and a few other
beasties.  I was concentrating on the beasties, and my pet went for the
vortex.  After a few bashes, it changed again.  I got the message 'the
red dragon hits the vortex' and then, zap, the world collapsed.  I
decided that maybe pet shapechangers were a bad idea, chalked it up to
that, and made a note to be more careful about what I tamed in the
future.

Last night, though, I had a similar collapse, this time when my tame
just-plain jackal was trading blows with a vortex.  I was just
watching, because I was trying on some new armor I'd just found.
Again, after a period of battle, the dungeon collapsed.  The vortex
seems to be the common element.  Judging from the timing, I suspect
that the problem comes when a swallowing monster tries to swallow a
pet.  This ring any bells?

